        (2, 'for the common people. Villages were called upon to supply soldiers,', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 267.1, 318.3, 278.6),
        (2, 'and the forced recruitment in rural areas caused widespread anger.', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 283.0, 318.1, 294.6),
        (2, 'Then in 1918-19 and 1920-21, crops failed in many parts of India,', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 299.0, 318.3, 310.5),
        (2, 'resulting in acute shortages of food. This was accompanied by an', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 315.1, 318.3, 326.6),
        (2, 'influenza epidemic. According to the census of 1921, 12 to 13 million', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 331.1, 318.3, 342.6),
        (2, 'people perished as a result of famines and the epidemic.', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 347.0, 278.9, 358.5),
        (2, 'People hoped that their hardships would end after the war was', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 370.3, 318.3, 381.8),
        (2, 'over. But that did not happen.', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 386.3, 163.4, 397.8),
        (2, 'At this stage a new leader appeared and suggested a new mode', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 409.4, 318.3, 420.9),
        (2, 'of struggle.', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 425.5, 84.6, 437.0),
        (2, '1.1 The Idea of Satyagraha', 12.0, 'RotisSansSerif-ExtraBold', True, 2301728, 34.3, 462.3, 169.2, 474.3),
        (2, 'Mahatma Gandhi returned to India in January 1915. As you know,', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 486.2, 318.1, 497.7),
        (2, 'he had come from South Africa where he had successfully fought', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 34.3, 502.3, 318.3, 513.8),
        (2, 'New words', 11.5, 'TT275T00', False, 2301728, 337.9, 302.5, 392.6, 314.0),
        (2, 'Forced recruitment – A process by which the', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 337.9, 325.6, 532.8, 337.1),
        (2, 'colonial state forced people to join the army', 11.5, 'TT274T00', False, 2301728, 337.9, 341.7, 528.2, 353.2),
        (2, 'Fig. 2 – Indian workers in South', 9.0, 'TT5CBT00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 622.2, 516.5, 631.2),
        (2, 'Africa march through Volksrust, 6', 9.0, 'TT5CBT00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 633.0, 523.3, 642.0),
        (2, 'November 1913.', 9.0, 'TT5CBT00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 643.8, 454.3, 652.8),
        (2, 'Mahatma Gandhi was leading the', 9.0, 'TT5C9T00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 654.6, 519.7, 663.6),
        (2, 'workers from Newcastle to', 9.0, 'TT5C9T00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 665.4, 492.5, 674.4),
        (2, 'Transvaal. When the marchers were', 9.0, 'TT5C9T00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 676.2, 530.2, 685.2),
        (2, 'stopped and Gandhiji arrested,', 9.0, 'TT5C9T00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 687.0, 508.4, 696.0),
        (2, 'thousands of more workers joined', 9.0, 'TT5C9T00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 697.8, 522.6, 706.8),
        (2, 'the satyagraha against racist laws', 9.0, 'TT5C9T00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 708.6, 524.9, 717.6),
        (2, 'that denied rights to non-whites.', 9.0, 'TT5C9T00', False, 2301728, 382.3, 719.4, 520.4, 728.4),
        (2, 'Reprint 2026-27', 8.0, 'Arial', False, 0, 259.3, 762.0, 316.7, 772.9),
        (3, '31', 8.0, 'Arial', False, 2301728, 531.4, 738.3, 540.2, 746.3),
        (3, 'Nationalism in India', 10.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 16777215, 559.7, 547.4, 569.7, 651.3),
        (3, 'the racist regime with a novel method of mass agitation, which he', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 60.2, 321.2, 71.7),
        (3, 'called satyagraha. The idea of satyagraha emphasised the power of', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 76.3, 321.2, 87.8),
        (3, 'truth and the need to search for truth. It suggested that if the cause', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 92.1, 321.1, 103.6),
        (3, 'was true, if the struggle was against injustice, then physical force was', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 107.9, 321.1, 119.4),
        (3, 'not necessary to fight the oppressor. Without seeking vengeance or', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 123.8, 321.1, 135.3),
        (3, 'being aggressive, a satyagrahi could win the battle through non-', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 139.9, 321.1, 151.4),
        (3, 'violence. This could be done by appealing to the conscience of the', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 155.7, 321.2, 167.2),
        (3, 'oppressor. People – including the oppressors – had to be persuaded', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 171.5, 321.1, 183.0),
        (3, 'to see the truth, instead of being forced to accept truth through the', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 187.4, 321.2, 198.9),
        (3, 'use of violence. By this struggle, truth was bound to ultimately', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 203.5, 321.1, 215.0),
        (3, 'triumph. Mahatma Gandhi believed that this dharma of non-violence', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 216.4, 321.4, 230.8),
        (3, 'could unite all Indians.', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 235.1, 130.4, 246.6),
        (3, 'After arriving in India, Mahatma Gandhi successfully organised', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 258.2, 321.1, 269.7),
        (3, 'satyagraha movements in various places. In 1917 he travelled to', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 274.3, 321.1, 285.8),
        (3, 'Champaran in Bihar to inspire the peasants to struggle against the', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 290.1, 321.1, 301.6),
        (3, 'oppressive plantation system. In 1918, Mahatma Gandhi went to', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 305.9, 321.1, 317.4),
        (3, 'Ahmedabad to organise a satyagraha movement amongst cotton', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 321.8, 321.1, 333.3),
        (3, 'mill workers. Then in 1918, he organised a satyagraha to support', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 337.9, 321.1, 349.4),
        (3, 'the peasants of the Kheda district of Gujarat. Affected by crop', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 353.7, 321.2, 365.2),
        (3, 'failure and a plague epidemic, the peasants of Kheda could not pay', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 369.5, 321.2, 381.0),
        (3, 'the revenue, and were demanding that revenue collection be relaxed.', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 385.4, 321.2, 396.9),
        (3, '1.2 The Rowlatt Act', 12.0, 'RotisSansSerif-ExtraBold', True, 2301728, 36.0, 419.5, 136.6, 431.5),
        (3, 'Emboldened with this success, Gandhiji in 1919 decided to launch a', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 446.1, 321.2, 457.6),
        (3, 'nationwide satyagraha against the proposed Rowlatt Act (1919). This', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 461.9, 321.2, 473.4),
        (3, 'Act had been hurriedly passed through the Imperial Legislative', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 477.8, 321.2, 489.3),
        (3, 'Council despite the united opposition of the Indian members. It', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 493.9, 321.1, 505.4),
        (3, 'gave the government enormous powers to repress political activities,', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 509.7, 321.2, 521.2),
        (3, 'and allowed detention of political prisoners without trial for two', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 525.5, 321.2, 537.0),
        (3, 'years. Mahatma Gandhi wanted non-violent civil disobedience against', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 541.4, 321.1, 552.9),
        (3, 'such unjust laws, which would start with a hartal on 6 April.', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 554.5, 290.9, 569.0),
        (3, 'Rallies were organised in various cities, workers went on strike in', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 580.5, 321.2, 592.0),
        (3, 'railway workshops, and shops closed down. Alarmed by the popular', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 596.3, 321.1, 607.8),
        (3, 'upsurge, and scared that lines of communication such as the railways', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 612.2, 321.2, 623.7),
        (3, 'and telegraph would be disrupted, the British administration decided', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 628.3, 321.2, 639.8),
        (3, 'to clamp down on nationalists. Local leaders were picked up from', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 644.1, 321.1, 655.6),
        (3, 'Amritsar, and Mahatma Gandhi was barred from entering Delhi.', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 659.9, 321.1, 671.4),
        (3, 'On 10 April, the police in Amritsar fired upon a peaceful procession,', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 675.8, 321.1, 687.3),
        (3, 'provoking widespread attacks on banks, post offices and railway', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 691.9, 321.2, 703.4),
        (3, 'stations. Martial law was imposed and General Dyer took command.', 11.5, 'Garamond', False, 2301728, 36.0, 707.7, 321.1, 719.2),
        (3, 'Mahatma Gandhi on Satyagraha', 9.0, 'Tahoma,Bold', True, 2301728, 341.3, 93.9, 490.7, 103.1),
        (3, '‘It is said of “passive resistance” that it is the', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 109.5, 535.9, 118.7),
        (3, 'weapon of the weak, but the power which is', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 121.5, 536.0, 130.7),
        (3, 'the subject of this article can be used only', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 133.5, 535.9, 142.7),
        (3, 'by the strong. This power is not passive', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 145.5, 536.0, 154.7),
        (3, 'resistance; indeed it calls for intense activity. The', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 157.5, 535.9, 166.7),
        (3, 'movement in South Africa was not passive', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 169.5, 535.9, 178.7),
        (3, 'but active …', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 181.5, 396.0, 190.7),
        (3, '‘ Satyagraha is not physical force. A satyagrahi', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 340.9, 197.1, 537.5, 206.3),
        (3, 'does not inflict pain on the adversary; he does', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 209.1, 536.0, 218.3),
        (3, 'not seek his destruction … In the use of', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 221.1, 535.9, 230.3),
        (3, 'satyagraha, there is no ill-will whatever.', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 340.9, 233.1, 501.0, 242.3),
        (3, '‘ Satyagraha is pure soul-force. Truth is the very', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 340.9, 248.7, 535.9, 257.9),
        (3, 'substance of the soul. That is why this force is', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 260.7, 535.9, 269.9),
        (3, 'called satyagraha. The soul is informed with', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 272.7, 536.0, 281.9),
        (3, 'knowledge. In it burns the flame of love. … Non-', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 284.7, 536.0, 293.9),
        (3, 'violence is the supreme dharma …', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 296.7, 481.4, 305.9),
        (3, '‘It is certain that India cannot rival Britain or', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 312.3, 536.0, 321.5),
        (3, 'Europe in force of arms. The British worship the', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 324.3, 536.0, 333.5),
        (3, 'war-god and they can all of them become, as', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 336.3, 536.0, 345.5),
        (3, 'they are becoming, bearers of arms. The', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 348.3, 535.9, 357.5),
        (3, 'hundreds of millions in India can never carry arms.', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 360.3, 536.0, 369.5),
        (3, 'They have made the religion of non-violence their', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 372.3, 536.0, 381.5),
        (3, 'own ...’', 9.0, 'Tahoma', False, 2301728, 341.3, 384.3, 372.7, 393.5),
        (3, 'Source', 18.0, 'Arial,BoldItalic', True, 16769196, 465.1, 383.6, 524.4, 401.6),
        (3, 'Source A', 10.0, 'Arial,BoldItalic', True, 2301728, 333.6, 59.3, 377.0, 69.3),
        (3, 'Read the text carefully. What did Mahatma', 9.0, 'Arial', False, 2301728, 342.7, 460.1, 512.4, 469.1),
        (3, 'Gandhi mean when he said satyagraha is', 9.0, 'Arial', False, 2301728, 342.7, 474.9, 514.6, 484.0),
        (3, 'active resistance?', 9.0, 'Arial', False, 2301728, 342.7, 490.1, 416.9, 499.1),
