        (1, 'Overview', 18.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 16627987, 75.0, 378.8, 140.4, 399.7),
        (1, 'The existence of social diversity does not threaten democracy. Political', 12.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 2301728, 75.0, 413.1, 431.4, 427.1),
        (1, 'expression of social differences is possible and sometimes quite desirable', 12.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 2301728, 75.0, 427.5, 431.4, 441.5),
        (1, 'in a democratic system. In this chapter we apply these ideas to the practice', 12.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 2301728, 75.0, 441.9, 431.3, 455.9),
        (1, 'of democracy in India. We look at three kinds of social differences that', 12.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 2301728, 75.0, 456.3, 431.3, 470.3),
        (1, 'can take the form of social divisions and inequalities. These are social', 12.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 2301728, 75.0, 470.7, 431.3, 484.7),
        (1, 'differences based on gender, religion and caste. In each case we look at', 12.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 2301728, 75.0, 485.1, 431.3, 499.1),
        (1, 'the nature of this division in India and how it gets expressed in politics.', 12.0, 'RotisSemiSerif', False, 2301728, 75.0, 499.5, 431.4, 513.5),
