        (211, 'In this chapter, we will explore the relationship between lines on a', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 106.8, 529.5, 503.5, 546.8),
        (211, 'plane surface. The table top, your piece of paper, the blackboard, and', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 92.4, 543.7, 503.5, 561.2),
        (211, 'the bulletin board are all examples of plane surfaces.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 92.4, 558.3, 402.1, 575.6),
        (211, 'Let us observe a pair of lines that meet each other. You will notice', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 106.8, 572.7, 503.5, 590.0),
        (211, 'that they meet at a point. When a pair of lines meet each other at a', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 92.4, 587.1, 503.5, 604.4),
        (211, 'point on a plane surface, we say that the lines intersect each other.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 92.4, 601.3, 483.5, 618.8),
