        (251, '12.1 Stars and Constellations', 17.0, 'NotoSans-SemiCondensedBo', True, 12270373, 71.4, 71.0, 297.8, 95.9),
        (251, 'At night, when we look up at the sky, we see', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 100.6, 365.8, 119.3),
        (251, 'many stars. Some stars are bright and others', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 116.6, 351.8, 135.3),
        (251, 'are dim. Stars shine with their own light.', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 132.1, 327.7, 150.8),
        (251, 'Some groups of stars appear to form', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 89.4, 147.6, 345.8, 166.3),
        (251, 'patterns which are like shapes of familiar', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 163.1, 346.8, 181.8),
        (251, 'things. Long ago, when watching stars in', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 178.6, 353.8, 197.3),
        (251, 'the night sky was a favourite pastime of our', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 194.1, 370.8, 212.8),
        (251, 'ancestors, they identified these star patterns with animals,', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 209.6, 431.7, 228.3),
        (251, 'things or characters in stories. Many cultures had names', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 225.1, 431.7, 243.8),
        (251, 'for patterns based on their own stories. These imaginary', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 240.6, 431.7, 259.3),
        (251, 'shapes helped them in recognising stars in the sky.', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 256.1, 387.7, 274.8),
        (251, 'Recognising stars and their patterns was a useful skill', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 89.4, 271.6, 431.7, 290.3),
        (251, 'for navigation in the olden times. Before the arrival of', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 287.1, 431.7, 305.8),
        (251, 'modern technology or even before the invention of the', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 302.6, 431.7, 321.3),
        (251, 'magnetic compass, it helped people, particularly sailors', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 318.1, 431.7, 336.8),
        (251, 'and travellers, in finding directions at sea or on land. It is', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 333.6, 431.7, 352.3),
        (251, 'still used in emergencies as a backup method.', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 349.1, 355.0, 367.8),
        (251, 'In earlier times, groups of stars forming patterns were', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 89.4, 364.6, 441.8, 383.3),
        (251, 'called constellations. Currently, the term constellation', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 380.1, 441.8, 398.8),
        (251, 'refers to defined regions of the sky that often include these', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 395.6, 441.8, 414.3),
        (251, 'patterns of stars. However, as the patterns of stars are often', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 411.1, 441.8, 429.7),
        (251, 'the most noticeable feature, the term constellation is still', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 426.6, 441.8, 445.2),
        (251, 'commonly used for these groups of stars.', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 442.6, 325.5, 461.2),
        (251, 'Do we find patterns', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 381.8, 117.2, 498.5, 134.5),
        (251, 'among the stars just', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 380.5, 131.2, 499.9, 148.5),
        (251, 'for fun or is there', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 387.3, 145.2, 493.0, 162.5),
        (251, 'some use of these', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 387.9, 159.2, 492.4, 176.5),
        (251, 'patterns?', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 411.6, 173.2, 465.6, 190.5),
        (251, 'Since different cultures denoted the constellation', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 104.4, 475.1, 391.7, 497.3),
        (251, 'boundaries in different ways, an internationally agreed', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 104.7, 490.5, 428.5, 513.3),
        (251, 'set of constellation boundaries were defined by the', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 104.9, 506.9, 403.4, 529.3),
        (251, 'International Astronomical Union (IAU) in the early', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 105.2, 522.8, 406.9, 545.3),
        (251, 'twentieth century. 88 constellations were officially', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 105.5, 539.0, 399.6, 561.3),
        (251, 'listed, thus, dividing the entire sky into 88 regions.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 105.8, 554.9, 403.2, 577.3),
        (251, 'These regions of sky are now defined as constellations.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 106.1, 570.6, 421.9, 593.3),
        (251, 'More to', 14.0, 'NotoSerif-ExtraBold', True, 12270373, 446.1, 552.7, 506.9, 574.2),
        (251, 'know!', 14.0, 'NotoSerif-ExtraBold', True, 12270373, 452.3, 570.4, 497.6, 591.7),
        (251, 'Some constellations are shown in Fig. 12.3. The stars', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 89.4, 604.3, 431.8, 623.0),
        (251, 'are joined by imaginary lines, drawn for easy identification.', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 620.3, 441.8, 639.0),
        (251, 'The constellation Orion is often represented as a hunter.', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 636.3, 441.7, 655.0),
        (251, 'There are three stars in the middle, which represent the belt', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 652.3, 441.8, 671.0),
        (251, 'of the hunter. Some people imagine that the hunter Orion,', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 668.3, 441.8, 687.0),
        (251, 'followed by his dog (constellation Canis Major), is battling', 13.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 71.4, 684.3, 441.8, 703.0),
