        (3, 'Vaishnavi says, “Here, Shubman performed better since his total is', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 107.5, 303.8, 504.3, 321.1),
        (3, '110 runs, while Yashasvi’s total is 96 runs”.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 318.8, 337.1, 336.1),
        (3, 'What do you think of Vaishnavi’s statement?', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 342.8, 347.0, 360.1),
        (3, 'Shreyas says, “But Yashasvi made 96 runs in 4 matches and Shubman', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 107.5, 361.8, 504.3, 379.1),
        (3, 'made 110 runs in 5 matches”.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 376.8, 261.5, 394.1),
        (3, 'So, how do we say who performed better? It is often not simple to compare', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 107.5, 391.8, 504.2, 409.1),
        (3, 'two groups of numbers and clearly say that one is better than the other.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 406.8, 483.5, 424.1),
        (3, 'Can a single number act as a representative of a group of numbers?', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 430.8, 485.2, 448.1),
        (3, 'For example, can we represent Shubman’s or Yashasvi’s batting in', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 445.8, 472.8, 463.1),
        (3, 'this series with one number? Discuss.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 460.8, 310.4, 478.1),
        (3, 'We saw one way already — the total of the values in the group! But,', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 107.5, 479.8, 504.2, 497.1),
        (3, 'if the group sizes are different, then the total may not be an appropriate', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 494.8, 504.2, 512.1),
        (3, 'measure to compare.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 509.8, 216.6, 527.1),
        (3, 'In some matches, a player could have scored more and in other matches', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 107.5, 524.8, 504.2, 542.1),
        (3, 'less. A representative number for the group can be found by balancing', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 539.8, 504.2, 557.1),
        (3, 'out these highs and lows. For example, we can add up the runs scored in', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 554.8, 504.2, 572.1),
        (3, 'all the matches and divide the total by the number of matches played. We', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 569.8, 504.3, 587.1),
        (3, 'call this value the ‘average’ or ‘arithmetic mean’ of the given data.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 584.6, 470.5, 602.1),
        (3, 'Here, the average number of runs scored by a player in a match', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 107.5, 599.8, 504.2, 617.1),
        (3, '= [Total runs scored by the player in all the matches] ÷ [Number of', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 614.8, 504.2, 632.1),
        (3, 'matches played].', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 93.1, 629.8, 189.4, 647.1),
        (3, 'Average number of runs scored by Shubman in a match = 110 ÷ 5 = 21 runs.', 12.0, 'NotoSerif-Regular', False, 2301728, 98.9, 644.8, 495.3, 662.1),
