        (5, 'EVELOPMENT', 9.5, 'FolioMdBT', False, 7308738, 324.1, 694.3, 396.4, 703.8),
        (5, '22', 13.5, 'FolioMdBT', False, 16777215, 83.2, 691.5, 100.3, 705.0),
        (5, 'The various production activities in the primary, secondary and', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 83.8, 555.4, 94.3),
        (5, 'tertiary sectors produce a very large number of goods and', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 96.7, 555.4, 107.2),
        (5, 'services. Also, the three sectors have a large number of people', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 109.7, 555.4, 120.2),
        (5, 'working in them to produce these goods and services. The next', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 122.6, 555.4, 133.2),
        (5, 'step, therefore, is to see how much goods and services are', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 135.6, 555.4, 146.1),
        (5, 'produced and how many people work in each sector. In an', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 148.8, 555.1, 159.3),
        (5, 'economy there could be one or more sectors which are dominant', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 161.8, 555.4, 172.3),
        (5, 'in terms of total production and employment, while other sectors', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 174.7, 555.4, 185.2),
        (5, 'are relatively small in size.', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 187.7, 368.2, 198.2),
        (5, 'How do we count the various goods and services', 12.0, 'FolioBkBT,Bold', True, 2301728, 236.2, 207.5, 541.5, 219.5),
        (5, 'and know the total production in each sector?', 12.0, 'FolioBkBT,Bold', True, 2301728, 236.2, 220.4, 524.9, 232.4),
        (5, 'With so many thousands of goods and services produced, you', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 241.7, 555.4, 252.2),
        (5, 'might think this is an impossible task! Not only would the task', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 254.6, 555.4, 265.2),
        (5, 'be enormous, you might also wonder how we can add up cars', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 267.6, 555.4, 278.1),
        (5, 'and computers and nails and furniture. It won’t make sense!!!', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 280.8, 555.1, 291.3),
        (5, 'You are right in thinking so. To get around this problem,', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 254.2, 295.9, 555.1, 306.4),
        (5, 'economists suggest that the values of goods and services should', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 308.9, 555.4, 319.4),
        (5, 'be used rather than adding up the actual numbers. For example,', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 321.8, 555.4, 332.4),
        (5, 'if 10,000 kgs of wheat is sold at Rs 20 per kg, the value of', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 334.8, 555.2, 345.3),
        (5, 'wheat will be Rs 2,00,000. The value of 5000 coconuts at Rs', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 347.8, 555.4, 358.3),
        (5, '15 per coconut will be Rs 75,000. Similarly, the value of goods', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 360.7, 555.1, 371.2),
        (5, 'and services in the three sectors are calculated, and then added', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 373.9, 555.4, 384.4),
        (5, 'up.', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 386.9, 254.2, 397.4),
        (5, 'Remember, there is one precaution one has to take. Not every', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 254.2, 402.0, 555.4, 412.5),
        (5, 'good (or service) that is produced and sold needs to be counted. It', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 415.0, 555.3, 425.5),
        (5, 'makes sense only to include the final goods and services. Take,', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 427.9, 555.4, 438.5),
        (5, 'for instance, a farmer who sells wheat to a flour mill for Rs 20 per', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 440.9, 555.4, 451.4),
        (5, 'kg. The mill grinds the wheat and sells the flour to a biscuit', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 454.1, 555.4, 464.6),
        (5, 'company for Rs 25 per kg. The biscuit company uses the flour', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 467.0, 555.4, 477.6),
        (5, 'and things such as sugar and oil to make four packets of biscuits.', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 480.0, 555.4, 490.5),
        (5, 'It sells biscuits in the market to the consumers for Rs 80 (Rs 20', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 493.0, 555.4, 503.5),
        (5, 'per packet). Biscuits are the final goods, i.e., goods that reach the', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 505.9, 555.4, 516.4),
        (5, 'consumers.', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 518.9, 293.0, 529.4),
        (5, 'Why are only ‘final goods and services’ counted? In contrast', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 250.3, 534.2, 555.4, 544.8),
        (5, 'to final goods, goods such as wheat and the wheat flour in this', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 547.2, 555.4, 557.7),
        (5, 'example are intermediate goods. Intermediate goods are used', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 560.2, 555.4, 570.7),
        (5, 'up in producing final goods and services. The value of final', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 573.1, 555.4, 583.6),
        (5, 'goods already includes the value of all the intermediate goods', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 586.1, 555.4, 596.6),
        (5, 'that are used in making the final good. Hence, the value of Rs', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 599.0, 555.4, 609.6),
        (5, '80 for the biscuits (final good) already includes the value of', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 612.2, 555.4, 622.8),
        (5, 'flour (Rs 25). Similarly, the value of all other intermediate goods', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 625.2, 555.4, 635.7),
        (5, 'would have been included. To count the value of the flour and', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 638.2, 555.4, 648.7),
        (5, 'wheat separately is therefore not correct because then we would', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 651.1, 555.4, 661.6),
        (5, 'be counting the value of the same things a number of times.', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 664.1, 555.4, 674.6),
        (5, 'First as wheat, then as flour and finally as biscuits.', 10.5, 'Bookman', False, 2301728, 236.2, 677.0, 502.4, 687.6),
